  "description_html": "Size chart comparison between <b>some</b> of the largest described phorusrhacid species:\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#03505B\" title=\"#03505B\"> </b> <i>Kelenken guillermoi</i> → Height = ~3 metres (9.8 ft).<sup id=\"cite_ref-Tamb2013_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Tamb2013-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#34AB9A\" title=\"#34AB9A\"> </b> <i>Devincenzia pozzi</i> → With a 65 centimetres (26 in) long skull,<sup id=\"cite_ref-Tamb2013_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Tamb2013-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> size extrapolated after <i>Kelenken</i>.</li>\n<li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#BF4D28\" title=\"#BF4D28\"> </b> <i>Phorusrhacos longissimus</i> → Height = ~Equivalent to <i>Titanis</i>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#EEA959\" title=\"#EEA959\"> </b> <i>Titanis walleri</i> → Height = ~1.4–1.9 metres (4.6–6.2 ft).<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<p>Human for scale is 1.8 meters tall.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-Tamb2013-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Tamb2013_1-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Tamb2013_1-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">\"Neogene Birds of South America\" in   (2013) <i> South American and Antarctic Continental Cenozoic Birds</i>, Springer Briefs in Earth System Sciences, Springer, pp. 59–86  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-94-007-5467-6_7\">10.1007/978-94-007-5467-6_7</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-94-007-5466-9\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-94-007-5466-9\">978-94-007-5466-9</a>. </small></cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2003). \"Systematic revision of the Phorusrhacidae (Aves: Ralliformes)\". <i>Papéis Avulsos de Zoologia</i> <b>43</b> (4): 55–91. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1590/S0031-10492003000400001\">10.1590/S0031-10492003000400001</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2005). \"Titanis walleri: bones of contention\". <i>Bulletin of the Florida Museum of Natural History</i> <b>45</b> (4): 201–229. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.58782/flmnh.xumx1681\">10.58782/flmnh.xumx1681</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
